---
description: Read the generated codebase map before opening or grepping source
alwaysApply: true
---

Before you Read, Grep or Glob this repo: open `docs/agents/CODEMAP.md` (which file, ~4k
tokens). For a route, a capability string or a watch→phone command: `docs/agents/CONTRACTS.md`.
For a symbol: `grep -n '^| Name ' docs/agents/SYMBOLS.md`. For what a check proves:
`docs/agents/CHECKS.md`. Then open ONE file. For callers and blast radius use the
`codegraph` MCP tool (`codegraph_explore`) instead of a grep-and-read loop.

After you add a file, change a file's first comment line, add a top-level declaration, a
daemon route or a capability: `python3 scripts/codemap-index.py` and commit the result.
`scripts/check-codemap.sh` is red until you do. A new code file needs a one-line header
comment saying what it is; that line is its entry in the map.
